  {
   "sha": "9172a4d1fc5f60c871a540f57f8dac60ef6a6e0a",
   "node_id": "C_kwDOULaCxNoAKDkxNzJhNGQxZmM1ZjYwYzg3MWE1NDBmNTdmOGRhYzYwZWY2YTZlMGE",
   "commit": {
    "author": {
     "name": "PathGao",
     "email": "42336971+PathGao@users.noreply.github.com",
     "date": "2026-09-02T00:11:42Z"
    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "PathGao",
     "email": "42336971+PathGao@users.noreply.github.com",
     "date": "2026-09-02T00:11:42Z"
    },
    "message": "Editor textarea: write the composition overlay's scroll offsets after sizing it\n\nThe composition branch of `_render` wrote `scrollTop`/`scrollLeft` before\n`_doRender` gave the textarea its size for the row, while the\nnon-composition branch a few lines down does it the other way round. A\nscroll offset is clamped against the element's size at the time it is\nwritten, so the order the sibling branch uses is the one that cannot lose\npart of the write. No behavioural difference was measured for the jitter in\nmonaco-editor#4796 — with the short content there is nothing to scroll —\nthis only makes the two branches agree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
